It's a matter of taste whether you Lojbanise names by dropping the final 
vowel or adding a final consonant (BTW, the consonant doesn't have to be 
"s" - a lot of people go for "n").  I used both methods in the examples, 
and in this case it seemed better to drop the "e", since "porc" is 
distinctive enough, and in any case, a lot of people mispronounce the 
word that way.

